name: sim.importMesh
description: Imports a mesh from a file
luaSynopsis: list vertices, list indices = sim.importMesh(int fileformat, string pathAndFilename, int options, float identicalVerticeTolerance, float scalingFactor)
pythonSynopsis: float[] vertices, int[] indices = sim.importMesh(int fileformat, string pathAndFilename, int options, float identicalVerticeTolerance, float scalingFactor)
inputs:
1. fileformat: set to 0. Fileformat is automatically detected
2. pathAndFilename: the location of the file to import.
3. options: bit-coded: bit0 set (1): keep identical vertices, bit7 set (128): ignore up-vector coded in fileformat
4. identicalVerticeTolerance: has no effect. set to zero
5. scalingFactor: the scaling factor to apply to the imported vertices
outputs:
1. vertices: an array of vertice arrays. The import operation may generate several meshes depending on the fileformat
2. indices: an array of index arrays. The import operation may generate several meshes depending on the fileformat
